<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-WMC sells N.Z. oil unit for A$34 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-WMC sells N.Z. oil unit for A$34 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>WMC Ltd said on Thursday it had concluded the divestment of its local and overseas petroleum assets with the A$34 million sale of its New Zealand operations to Fletcher Challenge Energy Ltd.</p>
<p>The mining house said its New Zealand unit Western Mining Corp (NZ) Ltd was the 40 percent owner of the Kupe gas field joint venture.</p>
<p>It said it had already entered into contracts for the sale of its U.S. oil and gas assets for US$270.5 million and the A$221 million sale of the Australasian assets.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
